; the chemistry of materials used to build the physical world.
; construction chemistry is where molecular structure meets structural performance.
; every construction material has a chemistry that determines its properties:
; concrete cures via hydration (chemical reaction, not drying).
; steel rusts via oxidation (electrochemical reaction).
; glass forms via silicate network formation (melt → amorphous solid).
; lime plaster sets via carbonation (CO2 from air reacts with Ca(OH)2).
; wood burns via cellulose combustion. treated wood resists via impregnation.
; 
; the hierarchy:
; chemistry → material properties → structural performance → architecture
; the chemical bonds determine the mechanical strength.
; the mechanical strength determines the structural form.
; the structural form enables the architectural space.
; links to engineering

(kosha construction-varga
  (vishesa chemistry-varga)
  (swarupa subanta)
  (yukta calcium silicon aluminium iron covalent-bond ionic-bond civil-varga architecture)
  (sthita solid))
